  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-0338b9f8 Web logs overview\"**\n- URL: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-0338b9f8-web-logs-overview-3d8a3d0ed316\n- Six panels on the Kibana Sample Data Logs view:\n  - Total requests (count)\n  - Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n  - Average bytes per response (average of `bytes`)\n  - Requests over time (line, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n  - Responses by status code (pie, terms on `response.keyword`)\n  - Top requested URLs (table, terms on `url.keyword`)\n- Time range is the last 2 years, because I don't know when the sample data's timestamps fall.\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-0338b9f8 5xx spike\"**\n- ID: `7ba1f0e6-79a6-40ca-878f-f40ca16e54d4`, type `.es-query`, runs every 1m, enabled.\n- Condition: count of documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` where `response.keyword` matches `5*`, over a 5-minute window, fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- The rule's status is still \"pending\" because it hasn't completed a run yet. I haven't confirmed it evaluates correctly.\n\n**Things to check:**\n- I couldn't run ES|QL queries to inspect the actual status-code values. `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` is not set in this shell, and direct API calls return 401. I used the MCP tools instead, which are authenticated. The `5*` wildcard assumes `response.keyword` holds the status code as a string, which matches the field type in `describe_data_view`, but I haven't seen the values.\n- The rule may never fire if the sample data's timestamps are old. Its 5-minute window is relative to now.\n- I didn't open the dashboard in a browser, so I haven't visually confirmed that the panels render data.",
